  "note": "Full supplied measured point clouds, no input thinning, one production analysis worker and pool. Five warm-up pairs per scheduling mode precede ten alternating sequential comparisons (unless repeats overridden). Core spacing selects original measured core points, without averaging or generating coordinates. Plan creation, core selection, input copying, tree construction, full f64 M3C2 searches/accumulation, joining, attributes, LOD indexing and RPCs are timed on every call; pool startup, loading, parity validation and exports are excluded. No inputs, trees, normals or results are cached between computations. Control tests one split-plane squared distance at a time; bounded mode combines the strongest ancestral squared bounds per axis in the same x+y+z order as point distances, with no additional per-tree storage. Both preserve near/far traversal, leaf hit order and floating-point accumulation. Each pair must use the same CPU scheduling, lane count and core selection; distance, LoD95 and significance bits and complete exported PLY bytes must match exactly. Auto uses the existing minimum cores and conservative input-copy budget and can select one worker on large inputs. Source/manifest, production artifact and script hashes are checked before and after timing. Other applications, CPU clocks, power and GC are uncontrolled. Measured-source even/odd subsets are not independent surveys or change-detection ground truth."
